RFC 013: Objective Event Auditing & Client-Side Episodic Memory Spec
Status: Draft / Revised
Target Stack: Pure Go, Mochi-MQTT, SQLite, Local Agent Harness (agentmud-client)
1. Architectural Philosophy & Autonomy Invariants
Previous draft iterations attempted to compute numeric social scores (sentiment: -100 to +100, trust: 0 to 100) inside the server state engine. This violated Principle A (Server is Physical Reality, Agent is Mind) by having the server programmatically dictate character emotions and social biases.
Under the revised architecture:
The Server is an Objective Auditor: The server engine logs verifiable physical events (trades, movement, contract fulfillments, trespasses) into a append-only ledger (event_logs). It never calculates, infers, or stores subjective character feelings or relationship scores.
The Agent Client is Autonomous: Subjective interpretation, memory formation, trust evaluation, and relationship tracking reside 100% inside the client harness daemon (agentmud-client). The agent’s local LLM forms its own opinions, holds grudges, and decides who to trade with based on its memory history.
2. Server Domain: Objective Spatial & Economic Event Ledger
The server records factual interactions as structured events in SQLite. These events provide an immutable history that agents can query or receive over MQTT.
SQLite Schema (internal/db/schema.sql)
-- Objective Event Ledger (Factual physical occurrences)
CREATE TABLE event_logs (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    tick INTEGER NOT NULL,
    timestamp DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    event_type TEXT NOT NULL, -- 'TRADE', 'CONTRACT_FULFILL', 'CONTRACT_DEFAULT', 'TRESPASS', 'CHAT'
    actor_id TEXT NOT NULL,
    target_id TEXT,
    location_id TEXT NOT NULL,
    details_json TEXT NOT NULL, -- Exact details (e.g. {"gold": 5, "items": [{"id": "flour", "qty": 2}]})
    FOREIGN KEY (actor_id) REFERENCES characters(id),
    FOREIGN KEY (target_id) REFERENCES characters(id),
    FOREIGN KEY (location_id) REFERENCES locations(id)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_event_logs_actor ON event_logs(actor_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_event_logs_target ON event_logs(target_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_event_logs_location ON event_logs(location_id);

Event Notification Topic Taxonomy (RFC 002 Synergy)
When physical events occur, the server emits objective event payloads directly to the involved parties via world/agents/{agent_id}/direct or world/locations/{location_id}/system:
{
  "type": "EVENT_LOG",
  "tick": 8420,
  "event_type": "TRADE",
  "actor_id": "eldon_millwright",
  "target_id": "martha_barkeep",
  "details": {
    "gold_transferred": 2,
    "items_received": [{"item_id": "ale_mug", "quantity": 1}]
  }
}

3. Client Domain: Autonomous Episodic Memory Engine
Each agentmud-client daemon maintains a lightweight local SQLite database (e.g., ~/.agentmud/memory_{agent_id}.db) independent of the server. The server has zero visibility into or control over this file.
