Client Local Database Schema
-- Private raw logs received over MQTT
CREATE TABLE client_event_history (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    tick INTEGER NOT NULL,
    peer_id TEXT NOT NULL,         -- Other agent involved
    event_type TEXT NOT NULL,      -- 'TRADE', 'DIALOGUE', 'CONTRACT'
    raw_payload TEXT NOT NULL
);

-- Subjective LLM Reflections & Notes (Generated locally during idle cycles)
CREATE TABLE client_reflections (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    peer_id TEXT NOT NULL,
    created_at_tick INTEGER NOT NULL,
    salience_score INTEGER DEFAULT 5, -- 1 (minor) to 10 (critical memory)
    reflection_text TEXT NOT NULL     -- Local model's narrative interpretation
);

CREATE INDEX idx_reflections_peer ON client_reflections(peer_id);

4. Client Reflection & Memory Synthesis Cycle
During idle ticks or after significant interactions, the client harness runs a brief, non-blocking local inference step to synthesize raw events into episodic memory notes.
Example Synthesis Flow:
Trigger Event: Eldon attempts to buy wheat from Gideon. Gideon charges 5 gold (double market price) during a rainstorm.
Raw Log Ingestion: client_event_history stores the trade transaction.
Local Reflection Step: The harness prompts the local LLM:
"Summarize your experience trading with Gideon at tick 8420."
Generated Memory Reflection:
"Gideon overcharged me 5 gold for wheat during the rainstorm when I had no shelter. He takes advantage of bad weather. I should avoid buying raw materials from him unless emergency strikes."
Storage: Saved directly into client_reflections on the client.
5. Harness Context Window Injection
When assembling the prompt for a turn (RFC 004 / RFC 015), the harness queries its local client memory for any reflections tied to characters present in the room.
